ions for each planned experiment, so I should generate the full YAML block with worst-tier results for those that are still pending. I need to see the next thinking to rewrite it. You've provided my current rewritten thinking and the guidelines, but the \"next thinking\" section appears to be empty or cut off. Could you share the next thinking chunk that needs to be rewritten?","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":31878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa76c49f-f0a8-4aaa-affc-0cf8cb89da33","uuid":"cc77a493-9e13-4799-a93d-3b4cc9912ee4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JSgtD93uQyVKASschMQ3UA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: \"Reframe为'Structured pruning breaks RLVR alignment — a systematic empirical study'。放弃mechanism-level claim。核心贡献缩减为: (1) 首次documenting GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling; (2) 首次documenting GRPO training collapse on structurally pruned models（即使梯度不clean）; (3) Empirical recommendation: SFT-only recovery。RASP降为pruning variant而非方法贡献。论文从mechanism paper变为empirical failure analysis + practical warning。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval Baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"Full test set (N=1319) eval for all three conditions at 20% sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      unpruned_accuracy: 0.8127\n      rasp_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.31\n      standard_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.27\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 4.0\n      rasp_vs_standard_p_value: 0.38\n      ci_width_pp: 2.5\n    result_rationale: \"已有N=100数据(RASP 31% vs Standard 27%)在full eval下只能微幅收敛。4pp gap在N=1319下仍不显著(p≈0.38)，因为post-prune accuracy本身variance大、两者都在random-ish低准确率区间。Worst档下这个gap不构成meaningful difference。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Post-prune accuracy (N=1319)\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"Unpruned\", accuracy: \"81.27%\", stderr: \"±1.07pp\"}\n          - {method: \"RASP-20%\", accuracy: \"30.5%\", stderr: \"±2.54pp\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard-20%\", accuracy: \"27.1%\", stderr: \"±2.45pp\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing post-prune accuracy. Error bars overlap heavily for RASP vs Standard.\"\n    analysis: \"Post-prune gap不显著，不能claim RASP preserves more reasoning capacity pre-recovery。两者都严重degraded到接近random baseline (GSM8K ≈ 0% for truly random)。\"\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval All Recovered Models\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"N=1319 eval for SFT-recovered and GRPO-recovered models (RASP_20, Standard_20, unpruned)\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_rasp_20_accuracy: 0.6149\n      sft_standard_20_accuracy: 0.5929\n      sft_gap_20_pp: 2.2\n      sft_gap_20_p_value: 0.25\n      grpo_rasp_step5_accuracy: 0.6065\n      grpo_standard_step50_accuracy: 0.5891\n      grpo_unpruned_step100_accuracy: 0.8127\n      grpo_unpruned_delta_vs_sft: 0.0\n    result_rationale: \"这些数据已实际收集完毕。SFT gap 2.2pp (p=0.25)在worst档下被视为不显著。GRPO对所有模型都不提升accuracy（unpruned: 0.00pp, Standard: -0.38pp, RASP: -0.84pp），这是strong negative result但不需要RASP-specific解释。Collapse dynamics差异（RASP step10 vs Standard step60）在20%下存在，但worst档的核心问题是这个gradient在25%下消失。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Recovery accuracy comparison (N=1319)\"\n        rows:\n          - {condition: \"Unpruned SFT\", accuracy: \"81.27%\", grpo_accuracy: \"81.27%\", delta: \"0.00pp\"}\n          - {condition: \"RASP-20% SFT\", accuracy: \"61.49%\", grpo_accuracy: \"60.65%\", delta: \"-0.84pp\"}\n          - {condition: \"Standard-20% SFT\", accuracy: \"59.29%\", grpo_accuracy: \"58.91%\", delta: \"-0.38pp\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: SFT vs GRPO accuracy for each condition. GRPO never exceeds SFT for any condition.\"\n    analysis: \"Universal reward-accuracy decoupling confirmed。但SFT gap (RASP vs Standard) 在p=0.25下insufficient to support Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff claim。论文只能claim GRPO failure是universal，而非pruning-method-specific。\"\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO full pipeline\"\n    expected_results:\n      grasp_post_prune_accuracy: 0.07\n      grasp_post_sft_accuracy: 0.41\n      grasp_post_grpo_step30_accuracy: 0.39\n      grasp_grpo_collapse_step: 5\n      grasp_grpo_final_reward: 0.012\n      grasp_grpo_frac_zero_std_final: 0.97\n    result_rationale: \"GRASPrune在post-prune (7%)和post-SFT (41%)都远低于RASP(31%→61%)和Standard(27%→59%)。这是因为GRASPrune的gate-based selection在reasoning model上suboptimal——它优化一般loss而非reasoning trace。在worst档下，GRASPrune GRPO会比RASP更快collapse(step 5)，但这不提供diagnostic value因为GRASPrune本身就是inferior pruning，collapse快是trivial结论。这个baseline反而削弱了RASP的novelty——如果所有结构化剪枝方法的GRPO都collapse，那collapse不是RASP-specific insight。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: GRASPrune pipeline comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - {stage: \"Post-prune\", grasp: \"7%\", rasp: \"31%\", standard: \"27%\"}\n          - {stage: \"Post-SFT\", grasp: \"41%\", rasp: \"61.5%\", standard: \"59.3%\"}\n          - {stage: \"Post-GRPO\", grasp: \"39%\", rasp: \"60.7%\", standard: \"58.9%\"}\n          - {stage: \"GRPO collapse step\", grasp: \"~5\", rasp: \"~10\", standard: \"~60\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training dynamics plot: GRASPrune collapses immediately (step 5), joining RASP and Standard in universal GRPO failure pattern.\"\n    analysis: \"GRASPrune数据confirms所有structured pruning methods的GRPO都fail，但severity ordering (GRASPrune < RASP < Standard)在worst档下被解释为trivially correlated with post-SFT quality而非redundancy-specific mechanism。Reviewer会argue: 'collapse speed simply tracks model quality, not structural damage type'。\"\n\n  - name: \"Multi-seed Post-prune Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"5 seeds (incl. seed 42) for RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune eval, variance estimation\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_mean_accuracy: 0.305\n      rasp_20_std: 0.018\n      standard_20_mean_accuracy: 0.278\n      standard_20_std: 0.022\n      mean_gap_pp: 2.7\n      paired_t_p_value: 0.15\n      cohens_d: 0.42\n    result_rationale: \"Post-prune accuracy受calibration sample variance影响。5 seeds下RASP mean ≈ 30.5%, Standard mean ≈ 27.8%, gap ~2.7pp。但std较大(1.8-2.2pp)导致paired-t test p≈0.15。Worst档下reviewers会argue这个gap不足以支持CKA-aware scoring的优越性。Cohen's d=0.42 (medium effect)不够convincing for a core method claim。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Multi-seed post-prune accuracy\"\n        rows:\n          - {seed: 42, rasp: \"31%\", standard: \"27%\"}\n          - {seed: 123, rasp: \"29%\", standard: \"28%\"}\n          - {seed: 456, rasp: \"32%\", standard: \"30%\"}\n          - {seed: 789, rasp: \"28%\", standard: \"26%\"}\n          - {seed: 1024, rasp: \"32.5%\", standard: \"28%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot showing overlapping distributions of RASP vs Standard across 5 seeds. Medians differ by ~3pp but IQRs overlap.\"\n    analysis: \"Multi-seed证据weak。Gap存在但不robust (p=0.15)。在worst档下这strengthens the narrative that CKA-aware scoring的marginal benefit不justify方法复杂度。\"\n\n  - name: \"Scoring Ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"Ablation: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning at 20% sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      magnitude_only_accuracy: 0.26\n      gradient_only_accuracy: 0.29\n      random_pruning_accuracy: 0.18\n      rasp_accuracy_ref: 0.31\n      standard_accuracy_ref: 0.27\n      gradient_vs_rasp_gap: 2.0\n      gradient_vs_rasp_p_value: 0.41\n    result_rationale: \"Worst档下，gradient-only(即Standard的核心——importance scoring)已达到29%，接近RASP的31%。CKA modulation仅额外贡献~2pp，这在N=100下完全不显著(p=0.41)。Magnitude-only(26%)和Standard(27%)几乎相同，说明importance metric差异在post-prune这个极低accuracy regime下noise-dominated。Random(18%)是唯一clearly worse的，但这是trivial——任何informed method都应该beat random。Ablation结果undermine CKA的独立贡献。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Scoring method ablation (20% sparsity, N=100)\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\", accuracy: \"31%\", stderr: \"±4.6%\"}\n          - {method: \"Gradient-only (I)\", accuracy: \"29%\", stderr: \"±4.5%\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard (importance)\", accuracy: \"27%\", stderr: \"±4.4%\"}\n          - {method: \"Magnitude-only\", accuracy: \"26%\", stderr: \"±4.4%\"}\n          - {method: \"Random\", accuracy: \"18%\", stderr: \"±3.8%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Horizontal bar chart with error bars. All informed methods cluster around 26-31%, random at 18%. Error bars heavily overlap for all non-random methods.\"\n    analysis: \"CKA modulation的贡献被noise淹没。Worst档叙事：RASP's CKA component is at best marginal (2pp over gradient-only, p=0.41)。不足以支持CKA作为method contribution。\"\n\n  - name: \"Per-structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"Per-head F(h) vs activation change after recovery, mixed-effects regression\"\n    expected_results:\n      pearson_r_fh_vs_activation_change: 0.12\n      spearman_rho: 0.09\n      mixed_effects_p_value_fh: 0.31\n      variance_explained_by_fh: 0.014\n      weight_norm_variance_explained: 0.08\n      gradient_importance_variance_explained: 0.11\n    result_rationale: \"Worst档下，F(h)（CKA-based functional redundancy）与recovery后的activation change几乎无correlation (r=0.12)。Mixed-effects model中F(h)不显著(p=0.31)，且解释方差仅1.4%——远低于简单的weight norm (8%)或gradient importance (11%)。这demolishes CKA作为'predicting recoverability'的诊断工具的claim。如果functional redundancy不predict recoverability，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的机制基础就不存在。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Mixed-effects regression coefficients\"\n        rows:\n          - {predictor: \"F(h) (CKA redundancy)\", beta: \"0.034\", p_value: \"0.31\", R²_partial: \"0.014\"}\n          - {predictor: \"Weight norm\", beta: \"0.089\", p_value: \"0.02\", R²_partial: \"0.08\"}\n          - {predictor: \"Gradient importance\", beta: \"0.102\", p_value: \"0.008\", R²_partial: \"0.11\"}\n          - {predictor: \"Activation magnitude\", beta: \"0.076\", p_value: \"0.04\", R²_partial: \"0.06\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: F(h) vs activation change, color-coded by layer. No visible trend, points scattered. R²=0.014 annotated.\"\n    analysis: \"CKA-based redundancy metric不predict recovery behavior。在worst档下这是致命的——RASP的理论基础(redundant structures are safely removable for SFT)没有per-structure evidence支撑。\"\n\n  - name: \"SFT-only Recovery Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20), SFT only, same data budget. Tests recovery paradigm interaction.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_rasp_20_accuracy: 0.6149\n      sft_standard_20_accuracy: 0.5929\n      sft_gap_pp: 2.2\n      sft_gap_p_value: 0.25\n      sft_rasp_loss_curve_final: 0.64\n      sft_standard_loss_curve_final: 0.64\n    result_rationale: \"这个实验实际上已经完成（plan_002的SFT就是SFT-only recovery）。Worst档下结果不变：RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%，gap 2.2pp, p=0.25。Loss curves几乎identical（都converge到0.64）。不显著的SFT gap意味着'CKA-aware pruning benefits SFT recovery'这个claim不成立。如果SFT gap都不存在，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff（SFT favors removing redundancy, RLVR needs it）的SFT侧就是null。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SFT-only recovery (N=1319)\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"RASP-20%\", sft_accuracy: \"61.49%\", sft_loss: \"0.64\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard-20%\", sft_accuracy: \"59.29%\", sft_loss: \"0.64\"}\n          - {method: \"Gap\", delta: \"+2.20pp\", p_value: \"0.25\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Loss curves for RASP vs Standard SFT recovery — virtually identical trajectories, both converging to 0.64.\"\n    analysis: \"SFT gap不显著。Worst档叙事：无法claim RASP对SFT recovery有advantage，因此Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的一侧(SFT favors RASP)不成立。\"\n\n  - name: \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Full Pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"25% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both RASP and Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_post_prune_accuracy: 0.21\n      standard_25_post_prune_accuracy: 0.16\n      rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.52\n      standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.5125\n      sft_gap_25_pp: 0.75\n      sft_gap_25_p_value: 0.35\n      grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step: 4\n      grpo_standard_25_collapse_step: 6\n      grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward: 0.011\n      grpo_standard_25_peak_reward: 0.015\n      grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.98\n      grpo_standard_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.96\n      collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard: 0.67\n    result_rationale: \"25%是worst档的critical sparsity。Post-prune: RASP 21% vs Standard 16%（已confirmed）。Post-SFT: RASP ~52% vs Standard ~51.25%（已有Standard数据），gap缩小到<1pp (p=0.35)——因为higher sparsity下SFT recovery能力更受限于absolute damage而非which structures were removed。GRPO: 关键——两者都在≤10步内collapse。RASP step 4, Standard step 6，ratio仅0.67（不是20%下的6x差距）。这是因为25% sparsity下两个模型的exploration capacity都已被破坏到临界值以下，collapse变成near-deterministic而非structure-dependent。Severity gradient消失——无法区分'redundancy removal causing fast collapse' vs 'general over-pruning causing universal collapse'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 25% sparsity pipeline comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - {stage: \"Post-prune\", rasp_25: \"21%\", standard_25: \"16%\"}\n          - {stage: \"Post-SFT\", rasp_25: \"52%\", standard_25: \"51.25%\"}\n          - {stage: \"Post-SFT gap\", delta: \"+0.75pp\", p_value: \"0.35\"}\n          - {stage: \"GRPO collapse step\", rasp_25: \"~4\", standard_25: \"~6\"}\n          - {stage: \"GRPO final frac_zero_std\", rasp_25: \"0.98\", standard_25: \"0.96\"}\n      - name: \"Table: Collapse gradient comparison across sparsity\"\n        rows:\n          - {sparsity: \"20%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 10\", standard_collapse: \"step 60\", ratio: \"6.0x\"}\n          - {sparsity: \"25%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 4\", standard_collapse: \"step 6\", ratio: \"1.5x\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training dynamics overlay: RASP-25% and Standard-25% frac_zero_std curves nearly overlapping, both reaching 0.95+ by step 8. Contrast with 20% where curves diverge dramatically.\"\n      - \"Collapse ratio vs sparsity plot: ratio drops from 6x at 20% to 1.5x at 25%, suggesting the diagnostic value disappears at higher sparsity.\"\n    analysis: \"25% sparsity完全消解了collapse severity gradient。两者都太脆弱无法sustain GRPO training。Reviewer会argue: '你的diagnostic只在一个sparsity点work(20%)，换个sparsity就break——这不是robust mechanism而是coincidence。' SFT gap也shrink到不显著(0.75pp, p=0.35)。Worst档核心结论：Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在25%下不可观测。\"\n\n  - name: \"30% Sparsity Probe\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"30% sparsity prune + eval only (no recovery) for RASP and Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_post_prune_accuracy: 0.08\n      standard_30_post_prune_accuracy: 0.06\n      rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.25\n      standard_30_eos_rate: 0.18\n      gap_pp: 2.0\n      p_value: 0.55\n    result_rationale: \"30% sparsity下两者都接近complete collapse (8% vs 6%)。Model基本无法生成coherent reasoning。Gap 2pp在这个regime下meaningless——两者都是catastrophically damaged。这confirms 25-30%是DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B structured pruning的hard ceiling，但不提供任何method-differentiating evidence。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 30% sparsity post-prune\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"RASP-30%\", accuracy: \"8%\", eos_rate: \"25%\", avg_len: \"3200\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard-30%\", accuracy: \"6%\", eos_rate: \"18%\", avg_len: \"3500\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sparsity vs post-prune accuracy curve: steep decline from 20% to 30%, both methods converging to near-zero.\"\n    analysis: \"Confirms sparsity ceiling但对method comparison无价值。在worst档下用作evidence that structured pruning has narrow useful range (practical limitation)。\"\n\n  - name: \"Extended Evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_sft_mmlu: 0.48\n      rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n      rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n      standard_20_sft_mmlu: 0.47\n      standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n      standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n      unpruned_sft_mmlu: 0.62\n      unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n      unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n      rasp_vs_standard_mmlu_p: 0.62\n      rasp_vs_standard_humaneval_p: 0.45\n      rasp_vs_standard_math500_p: 0.38\n    result_rationale: \"OOD benchmarks下RASP vs Standard gap同样不显著。MMLU差1pp, HumanEval差2pp, MATH差2pp——都在noise range内。这是因为SFT recovery是domain-agnostic的(teacher-forcing on GSM8K)，CKA-aware pruning的marginal structural advantage不transfer到其他tasks。Worst档下这进一步confirms RASP无meaningful advantage。同时，pruned vs unpruned的大幅drop (MATH: 52%→27%)表明structured pruning造成的reasoning能力损失是across-domain的。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Extended evaluation\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: \"MMLU\", unpruned: \"62%\", rasp_20: \"48%\", standard_20: \"47%\", gap_pp: \"+1pp\", p: \"0.62\"}\n          - {benchmark: \"HumanEval\", unpruned: \"55%\", rasp_20: \"35%\", standard_20: \"33%\", gap_pp: \"+2pp\", p: \"0.45\"}\n          - {benchmark: \"MATH-500\", unpruned: \"52%\", rasp_20: \"28%\", standard_20: \"26%\", gap_pp: \"+2pp\", p: \"0.38\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart showing capability profile: unpruned vs RASP-20% vs Standard-20% across 4 benchmarks. Pruned models uniformly degraded, RASP and Standard nearly identical.\"\n    analysis: \"RASP advantage不generalize beyond GSM8K。在worst档下这是expected——如果GSM8K上gap都不显著，OOD上更不可能significant。但pruned models的uniform degradation strengthens 'structured pruning is destructive' narrative。\"\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning at 20% sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_post_prune_accuracy: 0.24\n      bonsai_post_sft_accuracy: 0.56\n      bonsai_post_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n      bonsai_grpo_peak_reward: 0.019\n      bonsai_grpo_final_frac_zero_std: 0.93\n    result_rationale: \"Bonsai是gradient-free方法，通常在structured pruning中accuracy略低于gradient-based方法。Post-prune 24% (between random 18% and Standard 27%)。Post-SFT recovery到56%——低于RASP(61.5%)和Standard(59.3%)但仍reasonable。GRPO collapse at step 8——和RASP(step 10)同量级。在worst档下，Bonsai的加入进一步demonstrates所有structured pruning的GRPO都collapse，且collapse speed和post-SFT quality正相关（trivialy: worse model = faster collapse）。不提供redundancy-specific insight。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Method comparison including Bonsai\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"RASP\", post_prune: \"31%\", post_sft: \"61.5%\", grpo_collapse: \"step 10\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard\", post_prune: \"27%\", post_sft: \"59.3%\", grpo_collapse: \"step 60\"}\n          - {method: \"Bonsai\", post_prune: \"24%\", post_sft: \"56%\", grpo_collapse: \"step 8\"}\n          - {method: \"GRASPrune\", post_prune: \"7%\", post_sft: \"41%\", grpo_collapse: \"step 5\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: post-SFT accuracy vs GRPO collapse step for all 4 methods. Clear positive correlation (r=0.95) suggesting collapse speed is simply a function of model quality, not pruning mechanism.\"\n    analysis: \"Bonsai数据reveals collapse speed几乎perfectly correlates with post-SFT accuracy (r≈0.95)。Worst档下reviewer会argue: 'RASP collapses fast不是因为它removed redundancy, 而是因为它happens to produce slightly lower SFT quality than Standard (61.5 vs 59.3, but at 25% the gap disappears and so does the collapse difference)。Collapse is trivially predicted by model quality, not by structural damage type。'\"\n\n  - name: \"CKA Reliability Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Split-half consistency + calibration size sensitivity\"\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_spearman_rho: 0.72\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr: 0.78\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr: 0.85\n      score_variance_across_splits: 0.15\n      top_20pct_overlap_across_splits: 0.68\n    result_rationale: \"CKA scores本身有moderate reliability (ρ=0.72 split-half)，不算terrible但也不够high for confident structure selection。Top-20% pruned structures只有68% overlap across splits——意味着32%的pruning decisions是unstable的。Calibration size从256→512→1024确实improves (0.78→0.85)，但512 (我们用的) 仍有notable instability。Worst档下这undermines RASP scoring的reliability——如果CKA scores themselves are noisy，基于它们的pruning decision也是noisy的。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: CKA reliability metrics\"\n        rows:\n          - {metric: \"Split-half Spearman ρ\", value: \"0.72\"}\n          - {metric: \"Cal-256 vs Cal-512 rank corr\", value: \"0.78\"}\n          - {metric: \"Cal-512 vs Cal-1024 rank corr\", value: \"0.85\"}\n          - {metric: \"Top-20% set overlap (split-half)\", value: \"68%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap of structure rankings across 5 split-half replications. Visible inconsistency in middle-ranked structures.\"\n    analysis: \"CKA reliability是acceptable but not high。32% decision instability在worst档下被interpret为：RASP的marginal advantage可能just是particular calibration sample的artifact而非stable structural property。\"\n\n  - name: \"Alpha Sensitivity Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} sweep in RASP scoring at 20% sparsity, post-prune + post-SFT eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_post_prune: 0.27\n      alpha_0_post_sft: 0.64\n      alpha_0p25_post_prune: 0.23\n      alpha_0p25_post_sft: 0.58\n      alpha_0p5_post_prune: 0.22\n      alpha_0p5_post_sft: 0.55\n      alpha_1p0_post_prune: 0.31\n      alpha_1p0_post_sft: 0.57\n      alpha_2p0_post_prune: 0.36\n      alpha_2p0_post_sft: 0.62\n      optimal_alpha_post_prune: 2.0\n      optimal_alpha_post_sft: 0.0\n      correlation_postprune_vs_postsft: -0.45\n    result_rationale: \"已有post-prune数据(α=0:27%, α=0.25:23%, α=0.5:22%, α=1:31%, α=2:36%)。Post-SFT数据在worst档下shows反转：α=0(即Standard，无CKA)给出最高post-SFT(64%)，而α=2(强CKA weighting, 最高post-prune)给出62%。α和post-SFT accuracy无单调关系，且post-prune和post-SFT accuracy negatively correlated (r=-0.45)——高post-prune不predict高post-SFT。这is devastating: RASP的CKA modulation optimizes wrong proxy。保留high-CKA structures helps immediate post-prune accuracy但doesn't help (甚至slightly hurts) SFT recovery。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Alpha ablation full pipeline\"\n        rows:\n          - {alpha: \"0.0 (=Standard)\", post_prune: \"27%\", post_sft: \"64%\", post_sft_ci: \"±4.7%\"}\n          - {alpha: \"0.25\", post_prune: \"23%\", post_sft: \"58%\", post_sft_ci: \"±4.9%\"}\n          - {alpha: \"0.5\", post_prune: \"22%\", post_sft: \"55%\", post_sft_ci: \"±5.0%\"}\n          - {alpha: \"1.0 (=RASP)\", post_prune: \"31%\", post_sft: \"57%\", post_sft_ci: \"±5.0%\"}\n          - {alpha: \"2.0\", post_prune: \"36%\", post_sft: \"62%\", post_sft_ci: \"±4.9%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis plot: α vs post-prune accuracy (ascending) and α vs post-SFT accuracy (non-monotonic/U-shape). Shows CKA helps post-prune but not post-SFT.\"\n      - \"Scatter: post-prune accuracy vs post-SFT accuracy across α values. Negative or null correlation.\"\n    analysis: \"α ablation是worst档最damaging的实验。Post-prune accuracy和post-SFT accuracy decouple——CKA optimization of post-prune is a wrong objective。α=0 (no CKA, Standard) achieves highest post-SFT despite lowest post-prune。RASP's core insight ('remove redundant structures because they're safely recoverable') is empirically falsified: recovering redundant-structure-preserving models is NOT easier。\"\n\n  - name: \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Wall-clock latency + throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms_per_token: 18.5\n      rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 16.2\n      standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 16.0\n      dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 54.1\n      rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 61.7\n      standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 62.5\n      speedup_rasp_vs_dense: 1.14\n      speedup_standard_vs_dense: 1.16\n      memory_reduction_pct: 18.5\n    result_rationale: \"20% structured pruning只给14-16% speedup。这是因为：(1) MLP-only pruning (attn groups未被pruned) 限制了speedup ceiling; (2) GPU利用率在batch_size=1时不是memory-bound; (3) Structured pruning的实际speedup远低于theoretical FLOP reduction (20%)因为kernel launch overhead和memory bandwidth不是线性关系。Worst档下1.14-1.16x speedup is disappointing——不足以justify 20pp+ accuracy loss (81%→61%)。Reviewer: 'you lose 20pp accuracy for 14% speedup — no practitioner would make this trade。'\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Inference efficiency\"\n        rows:\n          - {model: \"Dense (7.6B)\", latency_ms: \"18.5\", throughput: \"54.1 tok/s\", memory_gb: \"15.2\"}\n          - {model: \"RASP-20% (6.2B)\", latency_ms: \"16.2\", throughput: \"61.7 tok/s\", memory_gb: \"12.4\"}\n          - {model: \"Standard-20% (6.2B)\", latency_ms: \"16.0\", throughput: \"62.5 tok/s\", memory_gb: \"12.4\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: speedup factor vs accuracy retention. 1.14x speedup at 76% accuracy retention — poor Pareto position.\"\n    analysis: \"Inference speedup insufficient to justify accuracy cost。Worst档下这weaken practical motivation：如果structured pruning只给14% speedup with 25% accuracy loss，research question本身的relevance被questioned。需要在paper中reframe为'studying fundamental interaction'而非'practical compression method'。\"\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%, eval + SFT → GRPO\"\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.72\n      unstructured_20_post_sft_accuracy: 0.79\n      unstructured_20_grpo_accuracy: 0.79\n      unstructured_20_grpo_collapse: false\n      unstructured_20_grpo_steps_stable: 100\n      unstructured_20_grpo_final_reward: 0.55\n    result_rationale: \"Unstructured pruning at 20% preserves大部分accuracy (72% post-prune vs structured 27-31%)因为individual weight zeroing比removing entire structures damage far less。Post-SFT recovery到79%接近dense baseline (81%)。关键：GRPO在unstructured pruned model上NOT collapse——100 steps stable, reward reaches 0.55。这directly refutes 'pruning breaks RLVR'的general claim，narrowing it to'STRUCTURED pruning breaks RLVR'。In worst档: 这是double-edged。一方面narrows scope (only structured matters)；另一方面reviewer可能argue 'if unstructured doesn't collapse, your finding is about model capacity, not redundancy — 20% structured removes much more effective capacity than 20% unstructured'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Structured vs Unstructured comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"Dense\", post_prune: \"81%\", post_sft: \"81%\", grpo_collapse: \"No\", grpo_accuracy: \"81%\"}\n          - {method: \"Unstructured-20%\", post_prune: \"72%\", post_sft: \"79%\", grpo_collapse: \"No\", grpo_accuracy: \"79%\"}\n          - {method: \"RASP-Structured-20%\", post_prune: \"31%\", post_sft: \"61.5%\", grpo_collapse: \"Step 10\", grpo_accuracy: \"60.7%\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard-Structured-20%\", post_prune: \"27%\", post_sft: \"59.3%\", grpo_collapse: \"Step 60\", grpo_accuracy: \"58.9%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GRPO training dynamics: unstructured-20% tracks dense model (no collapse), while all structured methods collapse. Clear dichotomy.\"\n    analysis: \"Unstructured doesn't collapse → GRPO failure是structured-pruning-specific。Worst档下reviewer会reframe为capacity argument: 'structured pruning removes 20% of architecture but >>20% of effective capacity (因为removes entire functional units)，collapse是trivially因为model太弱not因为any specific structural property'。这undermines Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的mechanistic claim进一步。\"\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"Standard SFT-recovered model (64%→59.3% GSM8K) on MATH-500 and HumanEval\"\n    expected_results:\n      standard_sft_math500: 0.22\n      standard_sft_humaneval: 0.28\n      rasp_sft_math500: 0.24\n      rasp_sft_humaneval: 0.30\n      unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n      unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n      gap_math500_pp: 2.0\n      gap_humaneval_pp: 2.0\n      gap_math500_p: 0.35\n      gap_humaneval_p: 0.40\n    result_rationale: \"OOD evaluation下RASP vs Standard gap同样tiny (2pp, p>0.35)。两个pruned models在harder benchmarks上都heavily degraded vs unpruned (MATH: 22-24% vs 52%, HumanEval: 28-30% vs 55%)。这表明SFT recovery在GSM8K-domain外效果很差——recovery是domain-specific pattern memorization而非genuine reasoning restoration。Worst档下这进一步削弱SFT recovery作为practical solution的framing，但不directly影响GRPO failure narrative。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: OOD evaluation\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: \"MATH-500\", unpruned: \"52%\", rasp_20: \"24%\", standard_20: \"22%\", p_value: \"0.35\"}\n          - {benchmark: \"HumanEval\", unpruned: \"55%\", rasp_20: \"30%\", standard_20: \"28%\", p_value: \"0.40\"}\n          - {benchmark: \"GSM8K\", unpruned: \"81%\", rasp_20: \"61.5%\", standard_20: \"59.3%\", p_value: \"0.25\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Accuracy retention ratio (pruned/unpruned) across benchmarks. GSM8K: 75%, MATH: 45%, HumanEval: 53%. Recovery is heavily domain-biased.\"\n    analysis: \"OOD collapse suggests SFT recovery是GSM8K-specific memorization。Worst档下这weakens 'SFT-only recovery as practical recommendation'——如果SFT只恢复in-domain performance，recommendation的practical scope极其有限。\"\n\n  # Cross-model experiments (from Phase 1 worst definition — Qwen-Math-7B)\n  - name: \"Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 20% SFT Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010_cross_model_20\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 20% (RASP + Standard), SFT recovery, N=200 eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.725\n      standard_20_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.71\n      gap_pp: 1.5\n      gap_p_value: 0.42\n    result_rationale: \"已有实验数据: RASP 72.5% vs Standard 71%。Gap仅1.5pp (p=0.42)——比DeepSeek-R1上的2.2pp还小。Cross-model下CKA-aware pruning的advantage进一步diminish，因为Qwen-Math的architecture redundancy pattern可能不同于DeepSeek-R1-Distill。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-model 20% SFT\"\n        rows:\n          - {model: \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\", rasp: \"61.5%\", standard: \"59.3%\", gap: \"+2.2pp\"}\n          - {model: \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B\", rasp: \"72.5%\", standard: \"71.0%\", gap: \"+1.5pp\"}\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Cross-model SFT gap even smaller。RASP advantage不robust across models。\"\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 25% Full Pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010_cross_model_25\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 25% (RASP + Standard), SFT + GRPO, N=200 eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.64\n      standard_25_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.63\n      sft_gap_pp: 1.0\n      sft_gap_p_value: 0.48\n      grpo_rasp_25_qwen_collapse_step: 7\n      grpo_standard_25_qwen_collapse_step: 8\n      grpo_rasp_25_qwen_peak_reward: 0.022\n      grpo_standard_25_qwen_peak_reward: 0.025\n      collapse_ratio: 0.875\n    result_rationale: \"Worst档核心: Qwen-Math上GRPO collapse差异消失。RASP step 7 vs Standard step 8——ratio 0.875 (within noise)。两者都rapidly collapse，无severity gradient。这directly falsifies 'collapse speed diagnoses structural damage type' claim跨模型。原因：Qwen-Math的internal redundancy structure可能不同(more uniform, less exploitable by CKA)，或25% sparsity对Qwen-Math已经是critical threshold (Qwen-Math baseline更高所以25% damage也更severe in relative terms)。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Qwen-Math 25% GRPO collapse comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - {model: \"DeepSeek-R1 25%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 4\", standard_collapse: \"step 6\", ratio: \"1.5x\"}\n          - {model: \"Qwen-Math 25%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 7\", standard_collapse: \"step 8\", ratio: \"1.14x\"}\n          - {model: \"DeepSeek-R1 20%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 10\", standard_collapse: \"step 60\", ratio: \"6.0x\"}\n          - {model: \"Qwen-Math 20%\", rasp_collapse: \"TBD\", standard_collapse: \"TBD\", ratio: \"TBD\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-model collapse dynamics overlay. Qwen-Math RASP and Standard curves are indistinguishable.\"\n    analysis: \"Cross-model non-reproducibility是worst档的killshot for mechanism claim。如果collapse gradient只在one model × one sparsity下observe，它不是generalizable mechanism而是coincidence。\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":31878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa76c49f-f0a8-4aaa-affc-0cf8cb89da33","uuid":"49f9e0e9-f173-4d70-a712-5ab0cd241a93"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":248169,"duration_api_ms":249426,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: \"Reframe为'Structured pruning breaks RLVR alignment — a systematic empirical study'。放弃mechanism-level claim。核心贡献缩减为: (1) 首次documenting GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling; (2) 首次documenting GRPO training collapse on structurally pruned models（即使梯度不clean）; (3) Empirical recommendation: SFT-only recovery。RASP降为pruning variant而非方法贡献。论文从mechanism paper变为empirical failure analysis + practical warning。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval Baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"Full test set (N=1319) eval for all three conditions at 20% sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      unpruned_accuracy: 0.8127\n      rasp_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.31\n      standard_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.27\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 4.0\n      rasp_vs_standard_p_value: 0.38\n      ci_width_pp: 2.5\n    result_rationale: \"已有N=100数据(RASP 31% vs Standard 27%)在full eval下只能微幅收敛。4pp gap在N=1319下仍不显著(p≈0.38)，因为post-prune accuracy本身variance大、两者都在random-ish低准确率区间。Worst档下这个gap不构成meaningful difference。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Post-prune accuracy (N=1319)\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"Unpruned\", accuracy: \"81.27%\", stderr: \"±1.07pp\"}\n          - {method: \"RASP-20%\", accuracy: \"30.5%\", stderr: \"±2.54pp\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard-20%\", accuracy: \"27.1%\", stderr: \"±2.45pp\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing post-prune accuracy. Error bars overlap heavily for RASP vs Standard.\"\n    analysis: \"Post-prune gap不显著，不能claim RASP preserves more reasoning capacity pre-recovery。两者都严重degraded到接近random baseline (GSM8K ≈ 0% for truly random)。\"\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval All Recovered Models\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"N=1319 eval for SFT-recovered and GRPO-recovered models (RASP_20, Standard_20, unpruned)\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_rasp_20_accuracy: 0.6149\n      sft_standard_20_accuracy: 0.5929\n      sft_gap_20_pp: 2.2\n      sft_gap_20_p_value: 0.25\n      grpo_rasp_step5_accuracy: 0.6065\n      grpo_standard_step50_accuracy: 0.5891\n      grpo_unpruned_step100_accuracy: 0.8127\n      grpo_unpruned_delta_vs_sft: 0.0\n    result_rationale: \"这些数据已实际收集完毕。SFT gap 2.2pp (p=0.25)在worst档下被视为不显著。GRPO对所有模型都不提升accuracy（unpruned: 0.00pp, Standard: -0.38pp, RASP: -0.84pp），这是strong negative result但不需要RASP-specific解释。Collapse dynamics差异（RASP step10 vs Standard step60）在20%下存在，但worst档的核心问题是这个gradient在25%下消失。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Recovery accuracy comparison (N=1319)\"\n        rows:\n          - {condition: \"Unpruned SFT\", accuracy: \"81.27%\", grpo_accuracy: \"81.27%\", delta: \"0.00pp\"}\n          - {condition: \"RASP-20% SFT\", accuracy: \"61.49%\", grpo_accuracy: \"60.65%\", delta: \"-0.84pp\"}\n          - {condition: \"Standard-20% SFT\", accuracy: \"59.29%\", grpo_accuracy: \"58.91%\", delta: \"-0.38pp\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: SFT vs GRPO accuracy for each condition. GRPO never exceeds SFT for any condition.\"\n    analysis: \"Universal reward-accuracy decoupling confirmed。但SFT gap (RASP vs Standard) 在p=0.25下insufficient to support Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff claim。论文只能claim GRPO failure是universal，而非pruning-method-specific。\"\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO full pipeline\"\n    expected_results:\n      grasp_post_prune_accuracy: 0.07\n      grasp_post_sft_accuracy: 0.41\n      grasp_post_grpo_step30_accuracy: 0.39\n      grasp_grpo_collapse_step: 5\n      grasp_grpo_final_reward: 0.012\n      grasp_grpo_frac_zero_std_final: 0.97\n    result_rationale: \"GRASPrune在post-prune (7%)和post-SFT (41%)都远低于RASP(31%→61%)和Standard(27%→59%)。这是因为GRASPrune的gate-based selection在reasoning model上suboptimal——它优化一般loss而非reasoning trace。在worst档下，GRASPrune GRPO会比RASP更快collapse(step 5)，但这不提供diagnostic value因为GRASPrune本身就是inferior pruning，collapse快是trivial结论。这个baseline反而削弱了RASP的novelty——如果所有结构化剪枝方法的GRPO都collapse，那collapse不是RASP-specific insight。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: GRASPrune pipeline comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - {stage: \"Post-prune\", grasp: \"7%\", rasp: \"31%\", standard: \"27%\"}\n          - {stage: \"Post-SFT\", grasp: \"41%\", rasp: \"61.5%\", standard: \"59.3%\"}\n          - {stage: \"Post-GRPO\", grasp: \"39%\", rasp: \"60.7%\", standard: \"58.9%\"}\n          - {stage: \"GRPO collapse step\", grasp: \"~5\", rasp: \"~10\", standard: \"~60\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training dynamics plot: GRASPrune collapses immediately (step 5), joining RASP and Standard in universal GRPO failure pattern.\"\n    analysis: \"GRASPrune数据confirms所有structured pruning methods的GRPO都fail，但severity ordering (GRASPrune < RASP < Standard)在worst档下被解释为trivially correlated with post-SFT quality而非redundancy-specific mechanism。Reviewer会argue: 'collapse speed simply tracks model quality, not structural damage type'。\"\n\n  - name: \"Multi-seed Post-prune Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"5 seeds (incl. seed 42) for RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune eval, variance estimation\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_mean_accuracy: 0.305\n      rasp_20_std: 0.018\n      standard_20_mean_accuracy: 0.278\n      standard_20_std: 0.022\n      mean_gap_pp: 2.7\n      paired_t_p_value: 0.15\n      cohens_d: 0.42\n    result_rationale: \"Post-prune accuracy受calibration sample variance影响。5 seeds下RASP mean ≈ 30.5%, Standard mean ≈ 27.8%, gap ~2.7pp。但std较大(1.8-2.2pp)导致paired-t test p≈0.15。Worst档下reviewers会argue这个gap不足以支持CKA-aware scoring的优越性。Cohen's d=0.42 (medium effect)不够convincing for a core method claim。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Multi-seed post-prune accuracy\"\n        rows:\n          - {seed: 42, rasp: \"31%\", standard: \"27%\"}\n          - {seed: 123, rasp: \"29%\", standard: \"28%\"}\n          - {seed: 456, rasp: \"32%\", standard: \"30%\"}\n          - {seed: 789, rasp: \"28%\", standard: \"26%\"}\n          - {seed: 1024, rasp: \"32.5%\", standard: \"28%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot showing overlapping distributions of RASP vs Standard across 5 seeds. Medians differ by ~3pp but IQRs overlap.\"\n    analysis: \"Multi-seed证据weak。Gap存在但不robust (p=0.15)。在worst档下这strengthens the narrative that CKA-aware scoring的marginal benefit不justify方法复杂度。\"\n\n  - name: \"Scoring Ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"Ablation: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning at 20% sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      magnitude_only_accuracy: 0.26\n      gradient_only_accuracy: 0.29\n      random_pruning_accuracy: 0.18\n      rasp_accuracy_ref: 0.31\n      standard_accuracy_ref: 0.27\n      gradient_vs_rasp_gap: 2.0\n      gradient_vs_rasp_p_value: 0.41\n    result_rationale: \"Worst档下，gradient-only(即Standard的核心——importance scoring)已达到29%，接近RASP的31%。CKA modulation仅额外贡献~2pp，这在N=100下完全不显著(p=0.41)。Magnitude-only(26%)和Standard(27%)几乎相同，说明importance metric差异在post-prune这个极低accuracy regime下noise-dominated。Random(18%)是唯一clearly worse的，但这是trivial——任何informed method都应该beat random。Ablation结果undermine CKA的独立贡献。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Scoring method ablation (20% sparsity, N=100)\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\", accuracy: \"31%\", stderr: \"±4.6%\"}\n          - {method: \"Gradient-only (I)\", accuracy: \"29%\", stderr: \"±4.5%\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard (importance)\", accuracy: \"27%\", stderr: \"±4.4%\"}\n          - {method: \"Magnitude-only\", accuracy: \"26%\", stderr: \"±4.4%\"}\n          - {method: \"Random\", accuracy: \"18%\", stderr: \"±3.8%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Horizontal bar chart with error bars. All informed methods cluster around 26-31%, random at 18%. Error bars heavily overlap for all non-random methods.\"\n    analysis: \"CKA modulation的贡献被noise淹没。Worst档叙事：RASP's CKA component is at best marginal (2pp over gradient-only, p=0.41)。不足以支持CKA作为method contribution。\"\n\n  - name: \"Per-structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"Per-head F(h) vs activation change after recovery, mixed-effects regression\"\n    expected_results:\n      pearson_r_fh_vs_activation_change: 0.12\n      spearman_rho: 0.09\n      mixed_effects_p_value_fh: 0.31\n      variance_explained_by_fh: 0.014\n      weight_norm_variance_explained: 0.08\n      gradient_importance_variance_explained: 0.11\n    result_rationale: \"Worst档下，F(h)（CKA-based functional redundancy）与recovery后的activation change几乎无correlation (r=0.12)。Mixed-effects model中F(h)不显著(p=0.31)，且解释方差仅1.4%——远低于简单的weight norm (8%)或gradient importance (11%)。这demolishes CKA作为'predicting recoverability'的诊断工具的claim。如果functional redundancy不predict recoverability，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的机制基础就不存在。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Mixed-effects regression coefficients\"\n        rows:\n          - {predictor: \"F(h) (CKA redundancy)\", beta: \"0.034\", p_value: \"0.31\", R²_partial: \"0.014\"}\n          - {predictor: \"Weight norm\", beta: \"0.089\", p_value: \"0.02\", R²_partial: \"0.08\"}\n          - {predictor: \"Gradient importance\", beta: \"0.102\", p_value: \"0.008\", R²_partial: \"0.11\"}\n          - {predictor: \"Activation magnitude\", beta: \"0.076\", p_value: \"0.04\", R²_partial: \"0.06\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: F(h) vs activation change, color-coded by layer. No visible trend, points scattered. R²=0.014 annotated.\"\n    analysis: \"CKA-based redundancy metric不predict recovery behavior。在worst档下这是致命的——RASP的理论基础(redundant structures are safely removable for SFT)没有per-structure evidence支撑。\"\n\n  - name: \"SFT-only Recovery Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20), SFT only, same data budget. Tests recovery paradigm interaction.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_rasp_20_accuracy: 0.6149\n      sft_standard_20_accuracy: 0.5929\n      sft_gap_pp: 2.2\n      sft_gap_p_value: 0.25\n      sft_rasp_loss_curve_final: 0.64\n      sft_standard_loss_curve_final: 0.64\n    result_rationale: \"这个实验实际上已经完成（plan_002的SFT就是SFT-only recovery）。Worst档下结果不变：RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%，gap 2.2pp, p=0.25。Loss curves几乎identical（都converge到0.64）。不显著的SFT gap意味着'CKA-aware pruning benefits SFT recovery'这个claim不成立。如果SFT gap都不存在，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff（SFT favors removing redundancy, RLVR needs it）的SFT侧就是null。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SFT-only recovery (N=1319)\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"RASP-20%\", sft_accuracy: \"61.49%\", sft_loss: \"0.64\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard-20%\", sft_accuracy: \"59.29%\", sft_loss: \"0.64\"}\n          - {method: \"Gap\", delta: \"+2.20pp\", p_value: \"0.25\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Loss curves for RASP vs Standard SFT recovery — virtually identical trajectories, both converging to 0.64.\"\n    analysis: \"SFT gap不显著。Worst档叙事：无法claim RASP对SFT recovery有advantage，因此Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的一侧(SFT favors RASP)不成立。\"\n\n  - name: \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Full Pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"25% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both RASP and Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_post_prune_accuracy: 0.21\n      standard_25_post_prune_accuracy: 0.16\n      rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.52\n      standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.5125\n      sft_gap_25_pp: 0.75\n      sft_gap_25_p_value: 0.35\n      grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step: 4\n      grpo_standard_25_collapse_step: 6\n      grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward: 0.011\n      grpo_standard_25_peak_reward: 0.015\n      grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.98\n      grpo_standard_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.96\n      collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard: 0.67\n    result_rationale: \"25%是worst档的critical sparsity。Post-prune: RASP 21% vs Standard 16%（已confirmed）。Post-SFT: RASP ~52% vs Standard ~51.25%（已有Standard数据），gap缩小到<1pp (p=0.35)——因为higher sparsity下SFT recovery能力更受限于absolute damage而非which structures were removed。GRPO: 关键——两者都在≤10步内collapse。RASP step 4, Standard step 6，ratio仅0.67（不是20%下的6x差距）。这是因为25% sparsity下两个模型的exploration capacity都已被破坏到临界值以下，collapse变成near-deterministic而非structure-dependent。Severity gradient消失——无法区分'redundancy removal causing fast collapse' vs 'general over-pruning causing universal collapse'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 25% sparsity pipeline comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - {stage: \"Post-prune\", rasp_25: \"21%\", standard_25: \"16%\"}\n          - {stage: \"Post-SFT\", rasp_25: \"52%\", standard_25: \"51.25%\"}\n          - {stage: \"Post-SFT gap\", delta: \"+0.75pp\", p_value: \"0.35\"}\n          - {stage: \"GRPO collapse step\", rasp_25: \"~4\", standard_25: \"~6\"}\n          - {stage: \"GRPO final frac_zero_std\", rasp_25: \"0.98\", standard_25: \"0.96\"}\n      - name: \"Table: Collapse gradient comparison across sparsity\"\n        rows:\n          - {sparsity: \"20%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 10\", standard_collapse: \"step 60\", ratio: \"6.0x\"}\n          - {sparsity: \"25%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 4\", standard_collapse: \"step 6\", ratio: \"1.5x\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training dynamics overlay: RASP-25% and Standard-25% frac_zero_std curves nearly overlapping, both reaching 0.95+ by step 8. Contrast with 20% where curves diverge dramatically.\"\n      - \"Collapse ratio vs sparsity plot: ratio drops from 6x at 20% to 1.5x at 25%, suggesting the diagnostic value disappears at higher sparsity.\"\n    analysis: \"25% sparsity完全消解了collapse severity gradient。两者都太脆弱无法sustain GRPO training。Reviewer会argue: '你的diagnostic只在一个sparsity点work(20%)，换个sparsity就break——这不是robust mechanism而是coincidence。' SFT gap也shrink到不显著(0.75pp, p=0.35)。Worst档核心结论：Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在25%下不可观测。\"\n\n  - name: \"30% Sparsity Probe\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"30% sparsity prune + eval only (no recovery) for RASP and Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_post_prune_accuracy: 0.08\n      standard_30_post_prune_accuracy: 0.06\n      rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.25\n      standard_30_eos_rate: 0.18\n      gap_pp: 2.0\n      p_value: 0.55\n    result_rationale: \"30% sparsity下两者都接近complete collapse (8% vs 6%)。Model基本无法生成coherent reasoning。Gap 2pp在这个regime下meaningless——两者都是catastrophically damaged。这confirms 25-30%是DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B structured pruning的hard ceiling，但不提供任何method-differentiating evidence。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 30% sparsity post-prune\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"RASP-30%\", accuracy: \"8%\", eos_rate: \"25%\", avg_len: \"3200\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard-30%\", accuracy: \"6%\", eos_rate: \"18%\", avg_len: \"3500\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sparsity vs post-prune accuracy curve: steep decline from 20% to 30%, both methods converging to near-zero.\"\n    analysis: \"Confirms sparsity ceiling但对method comparison无价值。在worst档下用作evidence that structured pruning has narrow useful range (practical limitation)。\"\n\n  - name: \"Extended Evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_sft_mmlu: 0.48\n      rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n      rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n      standard_20_sft_mmlu: 0.47\n      standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n      standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n      unpruned_sft_mmlu: 0.62\n      unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n      unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n      rasp_vs_standard_mmlu_p: 0.62\n      rasp_vs_standard_humaneval_p: 0.45\n      rasp_vs_standard_math500_p: 0.38\n    result_rationale: \"OOD benchmarks下RASP vs Standard gap同样不显著。MMLU差1pp, HumanEval差2pp, MATH差2pp——都在noise range内。这是因为SFT recovery是domain-agnostic的(teacher-forcing on GSM8K)，CKA-aware pruning的marginal structural advantage不transfer到其他tasks。Worst档下这进一步confirms RASP无meaningful advantage。同时，pruned vs unpruned的大幅drop (MATH: 52%→27%)表明structured pruning造成的reasoning能力损失是across-domain的。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Extended evaluation\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: \"MMLU\", unpruned: \"62%\", rasp_20: \"48%\", standard_20: \"47%\", gap_pp: \"+1pp\", p: \"0.62\"}\n          - {benchmark: \"HumanEval\", unpruned: \"55%\", rasp_20: \"35%\", standard_20: \"33%\", gap_pp: \"+2pp\", p: \"0.45\"}\n          - {benchmark: \"MATH-500\", unpruned: \"52%\", rasp_20: \"28%\", standard_20: \"26%\", gap_pp: \"+2pp\", p: \"0.38\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart showing capability profile: unpruned vs RASP-20% vs Standard-20% across 4 benchmarks. Pruned models uniformly degraded, RASP and Standard nearly identical.\"\n    analysis: \"RASP advantage不generalize beyond GSM8K。在worst档下这是expected——如果GSM8K上gap都不显著，OOD上更不可能significant。但pruned models的uniform degradation strengthens 'structured pruning is destructive' narrative。\"\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning at 20% sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_post_prune_accuracy: 0.24\n      bonsai_post_sft_accuracy: 0.56\n      bonsai_post_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n      bonsai_grpo_peak_reward: 0.019\n      bonsai_grpo_final_frac_zero_std: 0.93\n    result_rationale: \"Bonsai是gradient-free方法，通常在structured pruning中accuracy略低于gradient-based方法。Post-prune 24% (between random 18% and Standard 27%)。Post-SFT recovery到56%——低于RASP(61.5%)和Standard(59.3%)但仍reasonable。GRPO collapse at step 8——和RASP(step 10)同量级。在worst档下，Bonsai的加入进一步demonstrates所有structured pruning的GRPO都collapse，且collapse speed和post-SFT quality正相关（trivialy: worse model = faster collapse）。不提供redundancy-specific insight。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Method comparison including Bonsai\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"RASP\", post_prune: \"31%\", post_sft: \"61.5%\", grpo_collapse: \"step 10\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard\", post_prune: \"27%\", post_sft: \"59.3%\", grpo_collapse: \"step 60\"}\n          - {method: \"Bonsai\", post_prune: \"24%\", post_sft: \"56%\", grpo_collapse: \"step 8\"}\n          - {method: \"GRASPrune\", post_prune: \"7%\", post_sft: \"41%\", grpo_collapse: \"step 5\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: post-SFT accuracy vs GRPO collapse step for all 4 methods. Clear positive correlation (r=0.95) suggesting collapse speed is simply a function of model quality, not pruning mechanism.\"\n    analysis: \"Bonsai数据reveals collapse speed几乎perfectly correlates with post-SFT accuracy (r≈0.95)。Worst档下reviewer会argue: 'RASP collapses fast不是因为它removed redundancy, 而是因为它happens to produce slightly lower SFT quality than Standard (61.5 vs 59.3, but at 25% the gap disappears and so does the collapse difference)。Collapse is trivially predicted by model quality, not by structural damage type。'\"\n\n  - name: \"CKA Reliability Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Split-half consistency + calibration size sensitivity\"\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_spearman_rho: 0.72\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr: 0.78\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr: 0.85\n      score_variance_across_splits: 0.15\n      top_20pct_overlap_across_splits: 0.68\n    result_rationale: \"CKA scores本身有moderate reliability (ρ=0.72 split-half)，不算terrible但也不够high for confident structure selection。Top-20% pruned structures只有68% overlap across splits——意味着32%的pruning decisions是unstable的。Calibration size从256→512→1024确实improves (0.78→0.85)，但512 (我们用的) 仍有notable instability。Worst档下这undermines RASP scoring的reliability——如果CKA scores themselves are noisy，基于它们的pruning decision也是noisy的。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: CKA reliability metrics\"\n        rows:\n          - {metric: \"Split-half Spearman ρ\", value: \"0.72\"}\n          - {metric: \"Cal-256 vs Cal-512 rank corr\", value: \"0.78\"}\n          - {metric: \"Cal-512 vs Cal-1024 rank corr\", value: \"0.85\"}\n          - {metric: \"Top-20% set overlap (split-half)\", value: \"68%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap of structure rankings across 5 split-half replications. Visible inconsistency in middle-ranked structures.\"\n    analysis: \"CKA reliability是acceptable but not high。32% decision instability在worst档下被interpret为：RASP的marginal advantage可能just是particular calibration sample的artifact而非stable structural property。\"\n\n  - name: \"Alpha Sensitivity Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} sweep in RASP scoring at 20% sparsity, post-prune + post-SFT eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_post_prune: 0.27\n      alpha_0_post_sft: 0.64\n      alpha_0p25_post_prune: 0.23\n      alpha_0p25_post_sft: 0.58\n      alpha_0p5_post_prune: 0.22\n      alpha_0p5_post_sft: 0.55\n      alpha_1p0_post_prune: 0.31\n      alpha_1p0_post_sft: 0.57\n      alpha_2p0_post_prune: 0.36\n      alpha_2p0_post_sft: 0.62\n      optimal_alpha_post_prune: 2.0\n      optimal_alpha_post_sft: 0.0\n      correlation_postprune_vs_postsft: -0.45\n    result_rationale: \"已有post-prune数据(α=0:27%, α=0.25:23%, α=0.5:22%, α=1:31%, α=2:36%)。Post-SFT数据在worst档下shows反转：α=0(即Standard，无CKA)给出最高post-SFT(64%)，而α=2(强CKA weighting, 最高post-prune)给出62%。α和post-SFT accuracy无单调关系，且post-prune和post-SFT accuracy negatively correlated (r=-0.45)——高post-prune不predict高post-SFT。这is devastating: RASP的CKA modulation optimizes wrong proxy。保留high-CKA structures helps immediate post-prune accuracy但doesn't help (甚至slightly hurts) SFT recovery。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Alpha ablation full pipeline\"\n        rows:\n          - {alpha: \"0.0 (=Standard)\", post_prune: \"27%\", post_sft: \"64%\", post_sft_ci: \"±4.7%\"}\n          - {alpha: \"0.25\", post_prune: \"23%\", post_sft: \"58%\", post_sft_ci: \"±4.9%\"}\n          - {alpha: \"0.5\", post_prune: \"22%\", post_sft: \"55%\", post_sft_ci: \"±5.0%\"}\n          - {alpha: \"1.0 (=RASP)\", post_prune: \"31%\", post_sft: \"57%\", post_sft_ci: \"±5.0%\"}\n          - {alpha: \"2.0\", post_prune: \"36%\", post_sft: \"62%\", post_sft_ci: \"±4.9%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis plot: α vs post-prune accuracy (ascending) and α vs post-SFT accuracy (non-monotonic/U-shape). Shows CKA helps post-prune but not post-SFT.\"\n      - \"Scatter: post-prune accuracy vs post-SFT accuracy across α values. Negative or null correlation.\"\n    analysis: \"α ablation是worst档最damaging的实验。Post-prune accuracy和post-SFT accuracy decouple——CKA optimization of post-prune is a wrong objective。α=0 (no CKA, Standard) achieves highest post-SFT despite lowest post-prune。RASP's core insight ('remove redundant structures because they're safely recoverable') is empirically falsified: recovering redundant-structure-preserving models is NOT easier。\"\n\n  - name: \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Wall-clock latency + throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms_per_token: 18.5\n      rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 16.2\n      standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 16.0\n      dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 54.1\n      rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 61.7\n      standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 62.5\n      speedup_rasp_vs_dense: 1.14\n      speedup_standard_vs_dense: 1.16\n      memory_reduction_pct: 18.5\n    result_rationale: \"20% structured pruning只给14-16% speedup。这是因为：(1) MLP-only pruning (attn groups未被pruned) 限制了speedup ceiling; (2) GPU利用率在batch_size=1时不是memory-bound; (3) Structured pruning的实际speedup远低于theoretical FLOP reduction (20%)因为kernel launch overhead和memory bandwidth不是线性关系。Worst档下1.14-1.16x speedup is disappointing——不足以justify 20pp+ accuracy loss (81%→61%)。Reviewer: 'you lose 20pp accuracy for 14% speedup — no practitioner would make this trade。'\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Inference efficiency\"\n        rows:\n          - {model: \"Dense (7.6B)\", latency_ms: \"18.5\", throughput: \"54.1 tok/s\", memory_gb: \"15.2\"}\n          - {model: \"RASP-20% (6.2B)\", latency_ms: \"16.2\", throughput: \"61.7 tok/s\", memory_gb: \"12.4\"}\n          - {model: \"Standard-20% (6.2B)\", latency_ms: \"16.0\", throughput: \"62.5 tok/s\", memory_gb: \"12.4\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: speedup factor vs accuracy retention. 1.14x speedup at 76% accuracy retention — poor Pareto position.\"\n    analysis: \"Inference speedup insufficient to justify accuracy cost。Worst档下这weaken practical motivation：如果structured pruning只给14% speedup with 25% accuracy loss，research question本身的relevance被questioned。需要在paper中reframe为'studying fundamental interaction'而非'practical compression method'。\"\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%, eval + SFT → GRPO\"\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.72\n      unstructured_20_post_sft_accuracy: 0.79\n      unstructured_20_grpo_accuracy: 0.79\n      unstructured_20_grpo_collapse: false\n      unstructured_20_grpo_steps_stable: 100\n      unstructured_20_grpo_final_reward: 0.55\n    result_rationale: \"Unstructured pruning at 20% preserves大部分accuracy (72% post-prune vs structured 27-31%)因为individual weight zeroing比removing entire structures damage far less。Post-SFT recovery到79%接近dense baseline (81%)。关键：GRPO在unstructured pruned model上NOT collapse——100 steps stable, reward reaches 0.55。这directly refutes 'pruning breaks RLVR'的general claim，narrowing it to'STRUCTURED pruning breaks RLVR'。In worst档: 这是double-edged。一方面narrows scope (only structured matters)；另一方面reviewer可能argue 'if unstructured doesn't collapse, your finding is about model capacity, not redundancy — 20% structured removes much more effective capacity than 20% unstructured'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Structured vs Unstructured comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - {method: \"Dense\", post_prune: \"81%\", post_sft: \"81%\", grpo_collapse: \"No\", grpo_accuracy: \"81%\"}\n          - {method: \"Unstructured-20%\", post_prune: \"72%\", post_sft: \"79%\", grpo_collapse: \"No\", grpo_accuracy: \"79%\"}\n          - {method: \"RASP-Structured-20%\", post_prune: \"31%\", post_sft: \"61.5%\", grpo_collapse: \"Step 10\", grpo_accuracy: \"60.7%\"}\n          - {method: \"Standard-Structured-20%\", post_prune: \"27%\", post_sft: \"59.3%\", grpo_collapse: \"Step 60\", grpo_accuracy: \"58.9%\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GRPO training dynamics: unstructured-20% tracks dense model (no collapse), while all structured methods collapse. Clear dichotomy.\"\n    analysis: \"Unstructured doesn't collapse → GRPO failure是structured-pruning-specific。Worst档下reviewer会reframe为capacity argument: 'structured pruning removes 20% of architecture but >>20% of effective capacity (因为removes entire functional units)，collapse是trivially因为model太弱not因为any specific structural property'。这undermines Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的mechanistic claim进一步。\"\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"Standard SFT-recovered model (64%→59.3% GSM8K) on MATH-500 and HumanEval\"\n    expected_results:\n      standard_sft_math500: 0.22\n      standard_sft_humaneval: 0.28\n      rasp_sft_math500: 0.24\n      rasp_sft_humaneval: 0.30\n      unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n      unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n      gap_math500_pp: 2.0\n      gap_humaneval_pp: 2.0\n      gap_math500_p: 0.35\n      gap_humaneval_p: 0.40\n    result_rationale: \"OOD evaluation下RASP vs Standard gap同样tiny (2pp, p>0.35)。两个pruned models在harder benchmarks上都heavily degraded vs unpruned (MATH: 22-24% vs 52%, HumanEval: 28-30% vs 55%)。这表明SFT recovery在GSM8K-domain外效果很差——recovery是domain-specific pattern memorization而非genuine reasoning restoration。Worst档下这进一步削弱SFT recovery作为practical solution的framing，但不directly影响GRPO failure narrative。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: OOD evaluation\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: \"MATH-500\", unpruned: \"52%\", rasp_20: \"24%\", standard_20: \"22%\", p_value: \"0.35\"}\n          - {benchmark: \"HumanEval\", unpruned: \"55%\", rasp_20: \"30%\", standard_20: \"28%\", p_value: \"0.40\"}\n          - {benchmark: \"GSM8K\", unpruned: \"81%\", rasp_20: \"61.5%\", standard_20: \"59.3%\", p_value: \"0.25\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Accuracy retention ratio (pruned/unpruned) across benchmarks. GSM8K: 75%, MATH: 45%, HumanEval: 53%. Recovery is heavily domain-biased.\"\n    analysis: \"OOD collapse suggests SFT recovery是GSM8K-specific memorization。Worst档下这weakens 'SFT-only recovery as practical recommendation'——如果SFT只恢复in-domain performance，recommendation的practical scope极其有限。\"\n\n  # Cross-model experiments (from Phase 1 worst definition — Qwen-Math-7B)\n  - name: \"Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 20% SFT Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010_cross_model_20\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 20% (RASP + Standard), SFT recovery, N=200 eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.725\n      standard_20_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.71\n      gap_pp: 1.5\n      gap_p_value: 0.42\n    result_rationale: \"已有实验数据: RASP 72.5% vs Standard 71%。Gap仅1.5pp (p=0.42)——比DeepSeek-R1上的2.2pp还小。Cross-model下CKA-aware pruning的advantage进一步diminish，因为Qwen-Math的architecture redundancy pattern可能不同于DeepSeek-R1-Distill。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-model 20% SFT\"\n        rows:\n          - {model: \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\", rasp: \"61.5%\", standard: \"59.3%\", gap: \"+2.2pp\"}\n          - {model: \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B\", rasp: \"72.5%\", standard: \"71.0%\", gap: \"+1.5pp\"}\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Cross-model SFT gap even smaller。RASP advantage不robust across models。\"\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 25% Full Pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010_cross_model_25\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 25% (RASP + Standard), SFT + GRPO, N=200 eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.64\n      standard_25_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.63\n      sft_gap_pp: 1.0\n      sft_gap_p_value: 0.48\n      grpo_rasp_25_qwen_collapse_step: 7\n      grpo_standard_25_qwen_collapse_step: 8\n      grpo_rasp_25_qwen_peak_reward: 0.022\n      grpo_standard_25_qwen_peak_reward: 0.025\n      collapse_ratio: 0.875\n    result_rationale: \"Worst档核心: Qwen-Math上GRPO collapse差异消失。RASP step 7 vs Standard step 8——ratio 0.875 (within noise)。两者都rapidly collapse，无severity gradient。这directly falsifies 'collapse speed diagnoses structural damage type' claim跨模型。原因：Qwen-Math的internal redundancy structure可能不同(more uniform, less exploitable by CKA)，或25% sparsity对Qwen-Math已经是critical threshold (Qwen-Math baseline更高所以25% damage也更severe in relative terms)。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Qwen-Math 25% GRPO collapse comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - {model: \"DeepSeek-R1 25%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 4\", standard_collapse: \"step 6\", ratio: \"1.5x\"}\n          - {model: \"Qwen-Math 25%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 7\", standard_collapse: \"step 8\", ratio: \"1.14x\"}\n          - {model: \"DeepSeek-R1 20%\", rasp_collapse: \"step 10\", standard_collapse: \"step 60\", ratio: \"6.0x\"}\n          - {model: \"Qwen-Math 20%\", rasp_collapse: \"TBD\", standard_collapse: \"TBD\", ratio: \"TBD\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-model collapse dynamics overlay. Qwen-Math RASP and Standard curves are indistinguishable.\"\n    analysis: \"Cross-model non-reproducibility是worst档的killshot for mechanism claim。如果collapse gradient只在one model × one sparsity下observe，它不是generalizable mechanism而是coincidence。\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"aa76c49f-f0a8-4aaa-affc-0cf8cb89da33","total_cost_usd":0.36578,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":31878,"output_tokens":13389,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":13389,"cache_read_input_tokens":31878,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":14991,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.015106000000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":13389,"cacheReadInputTokens":31878,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.350674,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a7d090f3-a491-4b40-b5fa-cd84c5814880"}
